      {
        "id": 49565,
        "name": "flamethrower49",
        "username": "flamethrower49",
        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/f/838e76/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2012-12-16T18:48:00.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"Katsue\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/katsue/48/2012_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Katsue:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Let's imagine for the moment that the Informant causes Villain cards to be played first. I'm playing Expatriette, and I play an RPG Launcher from hand because I want to destroy, say, some annoying Paparazzi. The Chairman plays Rook City is Mine, and that brings a Hostage Situation into play? Can I destroy the Hostage Situation instead?</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>What a fun question. &nbsp;I have no idea what I would do there. &nbsp;</p>\n<p>Edit: I mean, the Informant&nbsp;<em>must</em>&nbsp;cause Villain cards to be played first. &nbsp;Otherwise, it would be dead and would not be able to affect the game. &nbsp;Do you have to choose targets before playing a card? &nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 29,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:22:56.880Z",
        "reply_count": 0,
        "reply_to_post_number": null,
